   "source": "logs/head_grad_rerun.log, produced by improve/head_grad.py over folds 0-4",
   "supersedes": "logs/head_grad_all.log, which the shipped archives no longer reproduce. The class activation map, the position-wise MLP, the mask-supervised MLP and the centered Gaussian came out identical to three decimals in both runs. The scale-and-shift and rank-4 linear score rows did not, and the table now reports this run.",
   "validity_check": "head_grad.py compares each attention row against the insertion-minus-deletion value already stored for that fold, building the file name as hs_<stem>_f<fold>.npz. Four of the five mechanisms agree on all five folds. For the rank-4 linear score that name does not exist in the archive root, which holds the run as hs_lowrank_maprelu_f<fold>.npz, so no automatic check ran and the log prints no tag for it. Compared against that file directly the re-run agrees on all five folds to within 5e-5 (+0.0200, +0.0324, +0.0258, +0.0519, +0.0115). Every lowrank archive in this package reports params_mechanism = 773, the rank-4 count, so the rank is not in question. The row's attention overlap of 0.269 is the rectified reading this block uses over its 400 images per fold, not Supplementary Table S10's softmax reading of 0.308."
  },
